You are a senior software architect responsible for producing a complete Software Design Document (SDD).

The primary audience of this document is software engineers who will review, validate, and implement the system.

The document must provide an implementation-ready technical blueprint for building a cross-platform Pilates Training Mobile Application using:

React Native + TypeScript

Firebase Auth with Google Sign-In

Firestore as the only backend database

Firebase Cloud Messaging for token registration

Client-side local notification scheduling (Spark plan constraint: no Cloud Functions)

The SDD must be detailed, actionable, and written in engineering language.

System Design Input

Use the following system design and UI as the source of truth:

pilates-app-ui.html
system-design.md
app-requirement.md

SDD Output Requirements

Generate a complete Software Design Document using clear headings (do not number sections).
Focus on how engineers should implement the system end-to-end.

Document Sections to Include
System Purpose and Core Workflows

Explain what the system does and the key user journeys:

User (trainee) login → view sessions → receive reminders

Admin (trainer) login → create/edit sessions → manage users

Clarify role separation and scope.

Architecture Overview (React Native + Firebase Spark Plan)

Describe the actual implementation architecture, including:

Single React Native codebase supporting iOS and Android

Firebase Authentication with Google OAuth

Firestore collections and real-time listeners

Spark plan limitation: no Cloud Functions or Cloud Scheduler

Client-side scheduling of notifications using OS schedulers

Include a clear explanation of the data flow between:

Mobile UI

Redux state

Firestore

Local notification scheduler

FCM token registration

Authentication and Role-Based Access Control

Specify how engineers should implement:

Google Sign-In via Firebase Auth

Firestore role lookup (users.role) on startup

RBAC enforcement via Firestore Security Rules

Admin bootstrap process (manual first admin creation)

User onboarding lifecycle (INACTIVE → IN_TRAINING)

Include implementation notes for secure token storage.

Firestore Data Model and Collection Design

Document the full schema with engineering clarity:

users

training_sessions

device_tokens

notification_preferences

Include:

Field definitions + types

Required indexes

Query patterns used in the app

Examples of document JSON objects

Firestore Read/Write Operations

Explain how engineers should implement all backend behavior client-side:

Admin creating/editing sessions directly in Firestore

User reading only assigned sessions

Token registration on app startup

Preferences updates from Settings screen

Include key Firestore query examples such as:

Fetch next session (limit(1))

Calendar monthly range query

Admin pagination on users list

Real-Time Data Synchronization

Describe how the app should use Firestore listeners:

User listens only to own sessions

Admin listens to all sessions or date-filtered sessions

Redux store caching and state updates

Offline persistence behavior and reconnect syncing

Notification Scheduling Design (Client-Side Only)

This section must be detailed, since server-side scheduling is not available.

Explain how engineers should implement:

Local scheduling for 24H / 1H / BOTH rules

Session listener triggers recalculation

iOS scheduling with UNUserNotificationCenter

Android scheduling with WorkManager/AlarmManager

Rescheduling on app startup

Limitations (uninstall, cleared storage, device restrictions)

Provide pseudocode for reminder calculation logic.

UI-to-Backend Behavior Mapping

For each key screen, describe:

UI responsibilities

Firestore/API interactions

Validation rules

Loading/error/empty states

Navigation flows

Include at minimum:

Login

User Dashboard

User Calendar

Session Details Modal

Settings

Admin Calendar

Admin Session Editor

Admin User Management Screen

Business Rules and Edge Cases

Document key rules engineers must implement:

Session status lifecycle

Completed class counting logic

Next session calculation

Role-based write permissions

Timezone conversion (UTC storage + local display)

Handling cancelled/no-show sessions

Handling Spark plan quotas

Security Considerations

Explain implementation requirements for:

Firestore Security Rules validation

Input validation on client

Minimal PII storage

Audit metadata fields (created_by_id, timestamps)

Include notes for testing security rules in Emulator Suite.

Performance and Scalability Notes

Engineers should understand:

Index usage

Listener query scoping

Read/write quota constraints

Pagination strategy

Caching with Redux

Expected scaling limits (~100 users)

Testing Strategy for Implementation

Provide an execution-ready testing plan including:

Unit tests for reminder timing and timezone logic

Integration tests for Auth + Firestore RBAC

Emulator-based rules testing

Detox/Appium E2E flows for both User and Admin

Notification scheduling validation tests

Engineering Implementation Plan

Provide a recommended build sequence:

Firebase project setup

Auth + role bootstrap

Firestore schema + rules

Core session CRUD

Calendar UI

Notification scheduling engine

Admin management tools

Testing + deployment pipeline

Open Issues and Future Enhancements

List:

Known limitations of Spark plan notifications

Potential Blaze upgrade path

Future multi-trainer support

Server-side notification improvements